                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "0/10",
                    "Correctly identifies the proctoscope",
                    "Labels the barrel, tip, obturator and illumination system where present",
                    "Explains the difference between proctoscope, anoscope and sigmoidoscope",
                    "States at least four indications",
                    "Mentions important contraindications and precautions",
                    "Describes preparation, positioning and preliminary examination",
                    "Explains safe insertion and systematic withdrawal",
                    "Recognises normal and abnormal mucosal findings",
                    "Identifies complications and their prevention",
                    "Explains the limitations of the examination"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "proctoscope_group_15",
              "group_title": "Final exam tip",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Remember: Proctoscope = direct examination of the anal canal and distal rectum; obturator = facilitates insertion. Do not confuse it with a sigmoidoscope, which is designed to examine farther into the distal colon."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
